const title = "  JavaScript Strings Guide  ";
const slug = title.trim().toLowerCase().replaceAll(" ", "-");

console.log(slug); // "javascript-strings-guide"

`trim()` removes the surrounding spaces, `toLowerCase()` normalizes case, and `replaceAll(" ", "-")` replaces every remaining space. For production slugs, also collapse repeated separators and strip punctuation.

